# Every text file is checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the default of
# Git for Windows, and so of the windows-latest runner) rewrites each file to
# CRLF. Go source tolerates that, but whatever reads these files as data does
# not: scripts/module-pins.txt gained a trailing CR on its commit column (which
# the pin-versus-docs tests then rejected as "not a full commit"), shell scripts
# stop parsing under bash, and fixtures that spell out line endings change
# meaning. The index already holds LF throughout; this keeps the working tree
# the same as the index.
* text=auto eol=lf
